    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0361" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.504/397</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 913</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-11">June 11, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        29.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to despatch No. 889 of June 1,
                    1933 [<hi rendition="#italic">1934</hi>], I have the honor to enclose the
                    translation from the <hi rendition="#italic">Reichsgesetzblatt</hi>, Part I, No.
                    52 of May 16, 1934,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d219-f1"/> of the Law on the above
                    mentioned subject.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d219-f2"/> The Law authorizes the
                    President of the Reich Institute for Employment Agencies to issue decrees
                    enabling him to prevent the employment of laborers or employees in the districts
                    prescribed in the decrees, without his previous approval. Machinery for the
                    control of itinerant unemployed is thus established and authority is <pb
                        facs="0362" n="262" xml:id="pg262"/> granted which can limit agricultural
                    laborers to that industry unless they left it more than three years prior to the
                    issuance of the pertinent decree.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William E. Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d219-f1" n="53" xml:id="d219-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d219-f2" n="54" xml:id="d219-f2-content">
                <p>Law for the regulation of labor distribution.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
